=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play runall/refused ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: runall/refused$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. debian13 with$
# apt-daily-upgrade.timer disabled by the administrator: Auto$
# Updates refuses; Run All plans the rest (decision 2).$
$
# Run All ######################################################$
$
  Controls -----------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 Already as asked$
   -  SSH Login            Root login off$
   -  SSH Auth             Nothing asked$
   -  SSH Port             Already as asked$
   -  Firewall             Already as asked$
   -  DNS                  Set 2 nameservers$
   -  Auto Updates         Refused: apt-daily-upgrade.timer i...$
   -  AppArmor             Status only$
   -  Backups              Used, not changed$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Apply all            Plan, review, confirm$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# Auto Updates skipped: apt-daily-upgrade.timer is off, and$
# hardn leaves apt's timers to you. Run systemctl enable --now$
# apt-daily-upgrade.timer, then try again.$
$
# Apply all ####################################################$
$
  Run All ------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  SSH Login            Root login off$
   -  DNS                  Set 2 nameservers$
  [ ] dhcpcd may rewrite /etc/resolv.conf on a lease$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      @@ -0,0 +1,23 @@$
      +# hardn's boot unit (P-34 (c);$
      | docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs$
      +# it before it arms the revert timer of a change that$
      | could lock you out, and$
      +# removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.$
      +#$
      +# At boot, before sshd reads its files: re-arm the revert$
      | timer of a change$
      +# waiting for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its$
      | window, or roll the$
      +# change back when its deadline has passed. Ordering$
      | only: sshd starts$
      +# whatever this unit does.$
      +[Unit]$
      +Description=hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an$
      | unconfirmed change$
      +DefaultDependencies=no$
      +After=local-fs.target sysinit.target ufw.service$
      +Before=ssh.service ssh.socket sshd.service sshd.socket$
      | shutdown.target$
      +Conflicts=shutdown.target$
      +$
      +[Service]$
      +Type=oneshot$
      +RemainAfterExit=yes$
      +ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot$
      +TimeoutStartSec=7min$
      +$
      +[Install]$
      +WantedBy=multi-user.target$
      -not installed$
      +installed and enabled$
      $ systemd-analyze verify --recursive-errors=no$
      | /run/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Disallow root login$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn.$
      +# Set by hardn:$
      +PermitRootLogin no$
$
   -  Set the nameservers$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
      @@ -1,3 +1,4 @@$
       # Generated by dhcpcd from eth0.dhcp$
       search example.net$
      -nameserver 192.0.2.1$
      +nameserver 192.0.2.54$
      +nameserver 2001:db8::54$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
$
      ssh.service$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      sshd -T shows no root login$
$
      sshd -T$
      $ sshd -T$
$
  Apply this plan?$
$
  Type the hostname [web-01, 0 or q]: web-01$
$
  [+] Install hardn's boot unit    Done$
  [+] Disallow root login          Done$
  [+] Set the nameservers          Done$
  [+] Reload sshd (ssh.service)    Done$
  [+] sshd -T shows no root login  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 3:01$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
  Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx is rolled$
  back at 12:03:01 UTC. To undo it now, run$
  `sudo hardn rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx`.$
$
  Backup of /etc/resolv.conf kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Run All ######################################################$
$
  Controls -----------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 Change pending$
   -  SSH Login            Change pending$
   -  SSH Auth             Nothing asked$
   -  SSH Port             Already as asked$
   -  Firewall             Change pending$
   -  DNS                  Change pending$
   -  Auto Updates         Change pending$
   -  AppArmor             Status only$
   -  Backups              Used, not changed$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Apply all            Change pending$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: runall/refused$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on$
# web-01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order;$
# hardn's own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
   -  Armed the revert timer$
      $ systemd-run$
      | --unit=hardn-revert-20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
      | "--description=hardn: roll back change$
      | 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx unless confirmed"$
      | --on-active=180s --timer-property=AccuracySec=1s$
      | /usr/local/bin/hardn rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
   -  Applied: Disallow root login$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
$
   -  Applied: Set the nameservers$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
$
   -  Applied: Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$

